   "date": "2017-03-08T21:49:02Z",
   "subject": "Using stan to compare two groups in a contingency table like Chi-square test",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I was trying to perform something like chi-square test from stan. The results are some what different. What should I do to compare two binomial distributions ?<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        real theta1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        real theta2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        n1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> binomial</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theta1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        n2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> binomial</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theta2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><br><br>This is my R code<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">n1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">37</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>N1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">370</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>n2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">65</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>N2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">851</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;like_chi-square.stan&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;n1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;N1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;n2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;N2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> warmup </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">th1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> extract</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$theta1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> th2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> extract</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$theta2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        geom_histogram</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> th1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        geom_histogram</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> th2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;blue&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">extract</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$theta1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> extract</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$theta2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br>this gives .08<br><br><br>but the chi-square p value is .2<br><br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">m </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">37</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">333</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">65</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">786</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncol </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>chisq</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">test</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br>Did I do it wrongly ? or this difference is just due to the simulation ?<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
