  {
   "id": "tYJPrY7gAgAJ",
   "from": "Mike Lawrence",
   "author": "dae01c57a3c54a3a",
   "date": "2017-03-08T22:17:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Using stan to compare two groups in a contingency table like Chi-square test",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">When doing Bayesian inference, you want to look at the full distribution of the posterior, not just the mean (which is *not* analogous to a p-value in any event). <div><br></div><div>So you should do:<div><br></div><div>    summary(mean(extract(fit1)$theta1 &lt; extract(fit1)$theta2))</div><div><br></div><div>and maybe<br><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">    hist(mean(extract(fit1)$theta1 &lt; extract(fit1)$theta2))</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">If you&#39;re specifically interested in the hypothesis of zero difference between the probabilities, then you can see where zero falls relative to this distribution. If most of the mass is far away from zero, you can probably discount zero as a credible hypothesis.</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><br>--<br>Mike Lawrence<br>Graduate Student<br>Department of Psychology &amp; Neuroscience<br>Dalhousie University<br><br>~ Certainty is (possibly) folly ~</div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Mar 8, 2017 at 5:49 PM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">elmah...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I was trying to perform something like chi-square test from stan. The results are some what different. What should I do to compare two binomial distributions ?<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">{</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">int</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> N1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">int</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> n1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">int</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> N2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">int</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> n2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">}</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>parameters</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">{</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>        real theta1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>        real theta2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">}</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>model</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">{</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>        n1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> binomial</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">N1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> theta1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">);</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>        n2 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> binomial</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">N2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> theta2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">);</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">}</span></div></code></div><br><br>This is my R code<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">n1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">37</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>N1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">370</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>n2 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">65</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>N2 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">851</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>fit1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">  stan</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;like_chi-square.stan&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> data </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;n1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;N1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;n2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;N2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> chains </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">4</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> iter </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">4000</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> warmup </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1000</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>df </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> data</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">frame</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">th1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> extract</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fit1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">$theta1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> th2 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> extract</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fit1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">$theta2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">df</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>        geom_histogram</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">aes</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">x </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> th1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> col </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> fill </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>        geom_histogram</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">aes</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">x </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> th2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">col </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;blue&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> fill </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>mean</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">extract</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fit1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">$theta1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> extract</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">fit1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">$theta2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></div></code></div><br>this gives .08<br><br><br>but the chi-square p value is .2<br><br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> matrix</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">37</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">333</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">65</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">786</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> ncol </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>chisq</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">test</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></div></code></div><br>Did I do it wrongly ? or this difference is just due to the simulation ?<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div>"
